Rename the worktree you run it from: change the slug it is registered under, so
it routes as <new-slug>.<domain>. A slug is a lowercase hostname label: letters,
digits and inner hyphens, at most 63 characters. The registration and index
entry move to the new slug and any leftover route files are removed; `up` writes
them at the new hostname. The data directory, volumes and pinned ports are keyed
by the worktree's ID and stay as they are. It refuses a slug another worktree
holds in the same domain, the reserved slug "shared", and a worktree that still
has containers, running or stopped: run `berth down` first.

Usage:
  berth worktree rename <new-slug> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for rename

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to berth.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -V, --version         output the version number
